 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Inferred deterministic form of uniform sampling: there are (product of group sizes) * N^(K-2) ways to join K groups (N nodes) with K-1 cross-group edges into a tree (count 1 when K=1). rank (decimal string, 0 <= rank < count) selects one: peel mixed-radix digits e_i = rank mod |group i| for i = 0..K-1 (then divide), then p_j = rank mod N for j = 0..K-3 (then divide). Node list = groups concatenated in order; p_j names a node and its group forms a Pruefer sequence. Decoding: repeatedly take the smallest group not yet removed and no longer present in the rest of the sequence, emit [groups[leaf][e_leaf], node p_j], remove it; finally emit [groups[u][e_u], groups[v][e_v]] for the last two groups u < v. Drawing rank uniformly yields a uniform valid edge set.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk04-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
    "sha256": "a89e24047c803759797d87567f7e8fa71933dcdd2366d6a943dcde4c2d1b37a9",
    "selector": "/problems/15/inferred_spec"
   }
  ]
 },
 "contentScope": "authored",
